From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 18:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: route direct vports by peer

An MLO net device can span all three PPE direct-switch nodes, but a PPE
virtual port has only one static queue.  Use the APPE per-flow priority
profile to select an enqueue virtual port and therefore the PPE2TCL ring
of the station's association node.

Track authorized peer addresses against direct virtual ports, retain the
static queue as a single-link and unknown-peer fallback, and reject flow
installation when the selected node is stopped.  Disable installed flows
for one node before its ring is stopped and restore them after restart so
a shared MLO virtual port cannot keep forwarding into a quiesced ring.

Link: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-ppe/-/tree/87bb9b326dfe7ddafb2cc8bc588e74d552a2a9b5
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
